{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Balak saw</b> — came to demand the blood of Israel." "<b>son of Zippor</b> — swooped upon them like a bird (צפור) to curse them. And this is \"as a bird wandering from her nest, so a curse without cause shall not come\" (Proverbs 26:2). וירא — that he saw that anger stood against Moses. וירא — that the anger was darkened. We find ראייה as a term of understanding, as in \"and all the people saw\" (Exodus 20:15). And likewise שמיעה as a term of understanding, as in \"for Joseph heard\" (Genesis 48:1)."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {1 "The second וירא explanation reads למשה after חמה; the third reads מן משה in some witnesses. Translated hyper-literally without resolving the variant. The phrase נתקדרה חמה is obscure; rendered literally as 'the anger was darkened.'"}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:22:50.232755342Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}